.Dd 2026-11-08
.Dt LBTS-DESCRIBE 1
.\" Manual page created by:
.\" Guus Sliepen <guus@lightbts.info>
.Sh NAME
.Nm lbts describe
.Nd replace the description of a ticket
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm lbts describe
.Op Fl m Ar message
.Ar id
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The command replaces the description of an existing ticket.
Initially, the description of a ticket is the text of its first message.
.Pp
If the command is run interactively, an editor is invoked with the current description,
which can then be changed.
Otherwise, the new description is taken from the
.Fl m
option or from stdin.
If the description is not changed, the command fails.
.Pp
The new description is recorded as a message with the pseudo-header
.Ql Description: replace ,
so the earlier descriptions remain in the history of the ticket, as shown by
.Ql lbts show -v .
Such a message can also be sent by email.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl m Ar message
Use the given description instead of invoking an editor or reading one from stdin.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lbts 1 ,
.Xr lbts-show 1 .
